 all this universe is pervaded.","start":247.704,"dur":30.72,"words":[[0.1,0.113,"There"],[0.287,0.05,"is"],[0.338,0.388,"another"],[0.762,0.412,"eternal"],[1.188,0.562,"existence"],[2.225,0.4,"higher"],[2.675,0.113,"than"],[2.788,0.113,"the"],[2.9,0.512,"changeable"],[3.413,0.55,"material"],[3.962,0.388,"Nature"],[4.55,0.588,"Prakriti"],[5.75,0.175,"that"],[5.925,0.138,"does"],[6.088,0.25,"not"],[6.4,0.35,"perish"],[6.925,0.175,"when"],[7.138,0.275,"all"],[7.438,0.463,"created"],[7.938,0.325,"beings"],[8.3,0.388,"perish"],[9.775,0.225,"This"],[10.012,0.15,"is"],[10.175,0.375,"called"],[10.575,0.1,"the"],[10.738,0.45,"Eternal"],[11.188,0.362,"Being"],[12.588,0.2,"This"],[12.8,0.138,"is"],[12.938,0.425,"also"],[13.425,0.25,"said"],[13.688,0.138,"to"],[13.825,0.113,"be"],[14.0,0.087,"the"],[14.088,0.45,"supreme"],[14.588,0.388,"abode"],[15.975,0.287,"Those"],[16.275,0.138,"who"],[16.462,0.362,"attain"],[16.875,0.125,"My"],[17.087,0.438,"supreme"],[17.575,0.388,"abode"],[18.062,0.163,"do"],[18.238,0.2,"not"],[18.45,0.287,"take"],[18.762,0.237,"birth"],[19.05,0.287,"again"],[20.35,0.188,"This"],[20.55,0.425,"supreme"],[21.025,0.375,"abode"],[21.663,0.163,"O"],[21.925,0.512,"Arjuna"],[22.625,0.312,"is"],[22.938,0.613,"attainable"],[23.562,0.138,"by"],[23.8,0.562,"unswerving"],[24.387,0.487,"devotion"],[24.913,0.113,"to"],[25.038,0.138,"Me"],[25.575,0.287,"within"],[25.9,0.138,"which"],[26.075,0.275,"all"],[26.35,0.312,"beings"],[26.675,0.487,"exist"],[27.288,0.237,"and"],[27.587,0.125,"by"],[27.8,0.125,"which"],[27.962,0.312,"all"],[28.275,0.125,"this"],[28.413,0.537,"universe"],[29.05,0.2,"is"],[29.262,0.512,"pervaded"]]},{"b":12,"part":0,"text":"Two basic paths of departure after death","start":278.424,"dur":3.6,"words":[[0.1,0.163,"Two"],[0.338,0.362,"basic"],[0.75,0.375,"paths"],[1.15,0.1,"of"],[1.275,0.55,"departure"],[1.925,0.362,"after"],[2.288,0.275,"death"]]},{"b":13,"part":0,"text":"O Arjuna, now I shall describe different paths departing by which, after death, the yogis do or do not come back. Passing gradually, after death, through celestial controllers of fire, light, daytime, the bright lunar fortnight, and the six months of the northern solstice of the sun, yogis who know the Self attain supreme abode and do not come back to earth. Passing gradually, after death, through celestial controllers of smoke, night, the dark lunar fortnight, and the six months of southern solstice of the sun, the righteous person attains heaven and comes back to earth again. The path of light of Self-knowledge and the path of darkness of ignorance are thought to be the world’s two eternal paths. The former leads to salvation (Mukti, Nirvana), and the latter leads to rebirth.","start":282.024,"dur":50.928,"words":[[0.1,0.113,"O"],[0.312,0.512,"Arjuna"],[1.062,0.338,"now"],[1.475,0.037,"I"],[1.613,0.175,"shall"],[1.8,0.487,"describe"],[2.325,0.362,"different"],[2.712,0.362,"paths"],[3.125,0.5,"departing"],[3.663,0.113,"by"],[3.862,0.237,"which"],[4.425,0.325,"after"],[4.75,0.275,"death"],[5.438,0.125,"the"],[5.575,0.388,"yogis"],[5.987,0.237,"do"],[6.362,0.3,"or"],[6.713,0.138,"do"],[6.875,0.188,"not"],[7.1,0.188,"come"],[7.35,0.275,"back"],[8.637,0.362,"Passing"],[9.037,0.475,"gradually"],[9.75,0.35,"after"],[10.1,0.275,"death"],[10.637,0.412,"through"],[11.062,0.487,"celestial"],[11.562,0.487,"controllers"],[12.062,0.1,"of"],[12.175,0.35,"fire"],[12.975,0.312,"light"],[13.637,0.512,"daytime"],[14.475,0.113,"the"],[14.6,0.287,"bright"],[14.925,0.263,"lunar"],[15.213,0.525,"fortnight"],[16.225,0.15,"and"],[16.387,0.1,"the"],[16.5,0.212,"six"],[16.762,0.275,"months"],[17.075,0.1,"of"],[17.188,0.1,"the"],[17.3,0.287,"northern"],[17.65,0.438,"solstice"],[18.1,0.087,"of"],[18.2,0.125,"the"],[18.325,0.275,"sun"],[18.988,0.438,"yogis"],[19.438,0.113,"who"],[19.6,0.125,"know"],[19.775,0.075,"the"],[19.85,0.25,"Self"],[20.15,0.338,"attain"],[20.562,0.438,"supreme"],[21.038,0.375,"abode"],[21.525,0.212,"and"],[21.75,0.1,"do"],[21.863,0.163,"not"],[22.